    "name": "tulip-tree",
    "notes": "STRAIGHTNESS IS THE ONE THING THE LATTICE KEEPS. The leaf silhouette that names this tree -- squared off at the tip, as if cut -- is a leaf-scale mark and at 10 cm there are no leaves, only clumps. What survives is the stem: `trunk.wander` 0.05 and `trunk.lean_deg` 1.5, the least wandering broadleaf here, with `clear_frac` 0.55 so more than half the tree is clean bole. Against the crooked crowns either side of it in this pass that reads as a distinct tree, which is the test.\n\nThe crown is small for the height and held right at the top (`height_frac` 0.44, `center_frac` 0.80), which is what a forest-grown tulip tree looks like and also what makes it cheap at 35 m.",
